   Scenario: Toggle all reflects individual todo state
     Given the app has a todo "Buy groceries"
diff --git a/specs/toggle-todo.feature b/specs/toggle-todo.feature
index f9fea3f..233b4bb 100644
--- a/specs/toggle-todo.feature
+++ b/specs/toggle-todo.feature
@@ -3,14 +3,24 @@ Feature: Toggle todo completion
   I want to mark todos as complete or active by clicking their checkbox
   So that I can track my progress
 
-  Scenario: Marking a todo as complete
-    Given the app has a todo "Buy groceries"
-    When the user toggles the "Buy groceries" todo checkbox
-    Then the "Buy groceries" todo has class "completed"
-    And the todo count shows "0 items left"
+  Rule: Toggling a todo must not destroy and recreate its DOM node
 
-  Scenario: Unmarking a completed todo
-    Given the app has a completed todo "Buy groceries"
-    When the user toggles the "Buy groceries" todo checkbox
-    Then the "Buy groceries" todo does not have class "completed"
-    And the todo count shows "1 item left"
+    Scenario: Marking a todo as complete
+      Given the app has a todo "Buy groceries"
+      When the user toggles the "Buy groceries" todo checkbox
+      Then the "Buy groceries" todo has class "completed"
+      And the todo count shows "0 items left"
+
+    Scenario: Unmarking a completed todo
+      Given the app has a completed todo "Buy groceries"
+      When the user toggles the "Buy groceries" todo checkbox
+      Then the "Buy groceries" todo does not have class "completed"
+      And the todo count shows "1 item left"
+
+  Rule: Toggling preserves list item identity across the interaction
+
+    Scenario: Toggle does not replace the todo list item element
+      Given the app has a todo "Buy groceries"
+      And the app has a todo "Clean house"
+      When the user toggles the "Buy groceries" todo checkbox
+      Then the todo list item elements from before the toggle are still in the DOM
